Subject: [PATCH] Start writable uniform copies from the uniform's value

MilkDrop's HLSL compiler lets a preset shader assign to a global uniform, e.g.
"q18 = 1;" (q18 is _qe.y) or "time *= 0.4;" (time is _c2.x). The write goes to
a per-invocation copy that starts with the uniform's value and that every
function sees. ReplaceUniformsAssignments declared that copy as an
uninitialized local of each function and only renamed references after the
first write, so the bank's other components (q19 after "q18 = 1"), compound
assignments and writes in another function read undefined values.

Each assigned uniform now gets one global copy, declared after the uniform and
initialized from it at the start of main() through the generator's global
initializers, and every reference inside functions uses the copy. Writes
include ++/-- and out/inout arguments. Global initializers keep reading the
uniform, as they run before the shader body.

---
